hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.23.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * 0.23.2 could not be configured. A comment in the maintainer script
    mentioned the debhelper substitution token by name, and dh replaces that
    token wherever it appears, comments included - so the rest of that comment
    line was left behind as a command, postinst exited 127, and dpkg stopped
    with the package half-configured. The daemons kept running, because the
    section that starts them had already gone by, but nothing after that point
    ran: on an upgrade that included new routing, nginx was never reloaded.

    The comment no longer names the token. The package build now also checks
    the generated maintainer scripts rather than only the ones in the source
    tree: it refuses to build if a generated script is not valid shell, or if
    it still contains a substitution token. The source script was valid the
    whole time - only the generated one was broken - so checking the source is
    not enough to catch this class of fault.

