hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.11.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * auth: allow GET /capabilities without authentication. The endpoint was
    absent from auth.d/audiocontrol-auth.json, so it fell through to the
    manifest's default_tier of risky and nginx answered 401 on a gated
    device. That defeats the endpoint's own purpose: a client is told a 404
    means the daemon does not resize images, but a 401 leaves it unable to
    tell "not supported" from "not allowed", which is exactly the guessing
    the endpoint exists to remove. It sits beside /version in the
    unauthenticated GET tier, since it reports only which image sizes the
    build offers. POST /imagecache/variants/purge deliberately stays gated:
    it deletes files.

